; The expression language, as an independent library. It must NOT depend on
; [native]: [native] consumes [Expr.Value], so a dependency back would be a
; cycle, and the point of the split is that the language owns no tensor,
; storage or graph type. See .ai/native_expr_refactoring_design.md.
;
; Wrapped (dune's default), so consumers see [Expr.Axis], [Expr.Value], and
; never a global [Axis] or [Value] -- which is the collision that keeps this
; out of [native], where (wrapped false) puts every unit in one flat namespace.
;
; No ppx: nothing here is preprocessed, so `dune build lib/expr` really does
; prove the [core]+[fmt] dependency boundary. Tests live in test/expr.
;
; [Checked] is private: overflow-checked arithmetic is reached through [Eval]
; and [Intrinsic], never directly, so it has no place in the public namespace.

(library
 (name expr)
 (private_modules checked)
 (libraries core err_trace fmt))
